    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d31">

                <pb facs="0044" n="24" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg24"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 465.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-01-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January</hi> 26, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my instruction of the 16th
                    instant, No. 461, I have to inform you that, under the date of the 31st ultimo,
                    Mr. Lane, the consul of the United States at Vera Cruz, writes that on that date
                    he had received a verbal communication from Mr. Mansfield, the consul at
                    Tabasco, confirming the report that he is in prison there, and allowed no means
                    of communicating with his friends, and that his sentence is a year’s
                    imprisonment.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
